# Details

Keep optional, short explanations close to the thing they explain.

These are civica.uk reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use a disclosure for an uncommon term or a short explanation that only some people need. The summary should make the hidden topic clear before someone opens it.

## When not to use it

Do not hide an error, a required instruction, a device’s current state or information most users need. Simplify the page first rather than hiding every paragraph.

## Home Assistant adaptation

An Energy view can keep a definition of a measurement nearby without obscuring the actual value and unit. A device card may explain why an action needs permission, but the immediate unavailable reason must remain visible. Do not place a link or a button inside the summary.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Use native details and summary elements. Enter or Space operates the focused summary and its expanded state is exposed automatically. Keep nested heading levels meaningful and do not rebuild the whole disclosure whenever sensor values update.

